title:: BMMatrixGUI
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - a GUI for matrix classes
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMMatrixGUI provides a GUI for subclasses of link::Classes/Matrices/BMAbstractMatrix::. Inputs are represented on the vertical axis and outputs on the horizontal axis. link::Classes/Matrices/BMMatrixMenuGUI:: provides an alternative view.

See also: link::Classes/Matrices/BMAbstractMatrix::, link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractGUI::, link::Classes/Matrices/BMMatrixMenuGUI::

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create a new matrix GUI.

argument:: matrix
An instance of a subclass of link::Classes/Matrices/BMAbstractMatrix::.
argument:: name
An optional link::Classes/String:: or link::Classes/Symbol:: indicating the title of the window. If nil is passed the name of matrix will be used.


Examples

(
// make a speaker list
l = [[-30, 'L'], [30, 'R'], [0, 'C'], [-110, 'Ls'], [110, 'Rs']].collectAs({|el, i|
	BMSpeaker.newFromSpherical(el[1], i, el[0], 0, 2);
}, BMInOutArray);
)

// something to route
(
b = Bus.audio(s, 8);
x = { Out.ar(b, {|i| Ringz.ar(Dust.ar(3, 0.1), 300 * (i + 1), 2)} ! 8) }.play;
)

// make a matrix
m = BMAudioMatrix(b.asBMInOutArray(\ringzes), l, name: 'Routing');

s.meter; // so we can watch

m.connect('ringzes-1', 'L'); // make one connection manually

BMMatrixGUI(m); // now play with the GUI
